---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import CTABand from '../components/CTABand.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About Salet | Property reports and buyer-only buying agent | Saran Gandhi"
  description="Salet sells property reports to home buyers and investors in England: a £9 Basic report on any address, and sold prices, stamp duty and what to offer in the £19 full report, with a 30-day refund. Founded by Saran Gandhi, it also acts as a buyer-only buying agent."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="About"
    title="From the Indian Army to Amazon to your side of the table"
    lede="Salet tells home buyers and investors in England what a property is really worth before they offer, and acts only for the buyer when they want someone to do it for them."
    compact
  />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-16 lg:px-8 lg:py-24">
    <div class="grid gap-14 lg:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="prose-salet lg:col-span-7">
        <h2>What Salet does</h2>
        <p>
          Type any address in England and get the <a href="https://salet.uk/intelligence">Basic report</a> (£9):
          the energy certificate, floor area and every Land Registry sale at the address and in the postcode.
          The full <a href="/reports/buyer-intelligence/">Buyer Intelligence Report</a> (£19) shows what similar homes
          nearby really sold for, the price range that evidence supports, the stamp duty you will pay, local rents,
          flood risk, crime, planning and schools. The <a href="/reports/decision-pack/">Decision Pack</a> (£69) costs
          five likely prices to the pound, and the <a href="/reports/legal-pack/">Legal Pack Review</a> (£29) finds the
          hidden costs in an auction or sale legal pack. Every figure is dated and sourced from HM Land Registry, the EPC
          register, the Environment Agency, ONS and local planning records. Every paid report carries a 30-day full refund.
          <a href="https://salet.uk/sample/intelligence">See a sample report</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          For buyers who want someone to search, negotiate and manage the purchase, Salet also works as a
          <a href="/services/">buyer-only buying agent</a>. It never acts for sellers.
        </p>
        <h2>The arc</h2>
        <p>
          Saran Gandhi was commissioned as an officer in the Indian Army, where the standards were simple: know the
          ground, plan in writing, be accountable for the outcome. He then spent nine years at Amazon in Europe as a
          senior leader in operations, responsible for learning and development across a frontline workforce of more
          than 100,000 people, and owned the accuracy of delivery promises made to millions of customers.
        </p>
        <p>
          In 2026 he left to build his own firms. Salet is the property practice: the product of moving from India to
          the UK, buying and analysing property here, and watching intelligent, careful people accept worse purchases
          than they should, because every professional in the transaction was working for somebody else.
        </p>
        <h2>Why Salet exists</h2>
        <p>
          The UK system gives the seller an agent whose job is the highest price. It gives the buyer portals,
          opinions and pressure. For first-time buyers, investors and buyers from overseas the asymmetry is sharper
          still: unfamiliar process, unfamiliar pricing, and no one in the transaction paid to tell them the truth.
        </p>
        <p>
          Salet is the correction: the evidence a seller's agent has, put in the buyer's hands for the price of a
          takeaway, and a buying agent that acts only for the buyer, applies institutional discipline to ordinary
          purchases, and stays accountable after completion. It is a deliberately personal firm. You deal
          with the founder, his standards and his network, not an office of juniors.
        </p>
        <h2>The concierge philosophy</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Written beats verbal.</strong> Briefs, proposals, progress notes and reports, all in writing.</li>
          <li><strong>Evidence beats enthusiasm.</strong> Analysis first; viewings second; feelings last.</li>
          <li><strong>Bad news travels fastest.</strong> Problems reach you early, framed with options.</li>
          <li><strong>The relationship outlasts the transaction.</strong> The ladder of services exists so that accountability does not end at the keys.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <aside class="lg:col-span-5">
        <div class="reveal border border-line bg-ivory-2/60 p-8 lg:p-10">
          <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-green-2">Credentials</p>
          <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone">
            <li>Salet Ltd, registered in England and Wales, company no. 16662600</li>
            <li>Professional indemnity insurance held</li>
            <li>Founder: ex-Indian Army officer; nine years senior operations leadership, Amazon EU</li>
          </ul>
          <!-- TODO: add The Property Ombudsman and PropertyMark entries here once membership is actually held. Display nothing until then. -->
          <p class="mt-6 text-xs leading-relaxed text-mist">
            Salet provides property consulting and buyer representation. It does not provide financial, tax or
            investment advice, and does not market property or investments to the public.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal reveal-d1 mt-6 border border-line bg-ivory p-8 lg:p-10">
          <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-green-2">Direct line</p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone">
            Salet is founder-led by design. Questions land with the person accountable for the answer.
          </p>
          <a href="mailto:saran@salet.uk" class="mt-4 inline-block text-sm text-green-2 underline underline-offset-4">saran@salet.uk</a>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTABand />
</Base>
